WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
Picture a chariot.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:05.770
A driver holds the reins,
and the horses pull hard.

3
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.120
But someone else rides
in it, who never drives.

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:13.040
An ancient Hindu teaching
says that rider is the atman,

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.480
the true self.

6
00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.050
The body is only the chariot.

7
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.050
Elsewhere, a father has his
son dissolve salt in water,

8
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.050
then tells him: you are that.

9
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.630
So is your deepest self
a tiny part of God,

10
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.820
a separate soul, or
God itself in disguise?

11
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.450
In this mission, you'll
follow how those words,

12
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.990
you are that, have been read.

13
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.440
Then you'll ask the big question: are the
self and ultimate reality one, or two?

14
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:48.590
Your mission: find out how Hindus
answer what the deepest self really is.
